# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# fireux-deploy-ignore
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PURPOSE:
#   This file lists directory patterns that FireUX must EXCLUDE from production
#   builds. Any file matched here will be ignored by Nuxt during build via
#   configureDeployIgnore(), meaning:
#     - pages, layouts, components, and composables are NOT scanned
#     - no server or client bundles are generated for them
#     - Firebase hosting and Cloud Functions never receive the code
#
# DEFAULT BEHAVIOUR:
#   - If this file exists, FireUX uses these patterns.
#   - If it does not exist, FireUX defaults to ignoring '**/dev/**'.
#
# ENVIRONMENT OVERRIDES:
#   FIREUX_DEPLOY_IGNORE=<comma-separated globs>
#       Overrides this file entirely. Use sparingly.
#
#   FIREUX_DEPLOY_WITH_DEV=1
#       Disables ALL ignores. Use only for deep debugging.
#
# RECOMMENDED BASELINE:
#   Keep this simple. The entire FireUX dev system lives under /dev paths.
#   This single rule excludes all dev tooling across all packages:

**/dev/**

# OPTIONAL EXTRAS (uncomment if needed):
# **/__playground__/**
# **/.storybook/**
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
